From d559bb7ee3e1c1aea8eb673712efe0f20bc774af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Spatiand build <claude@prasetya.id>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 09:33:18 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 20/22] Spatiand: each window says what it shows, for the
 room's dictation and assistant

The room asks a window what it shows (spatiand_xr_surface_v1.describe, since version 9 of Spatiand's
own protocol, crates/spatiand-proto in Spatiand): dictation leans its spelling towards a page's words,
and the assistant reads a window through it. Every toplevel now has the protocol's object
(ui/ozone/platform/wayland/host/spatiand_xr.cc) and nothing else of it is asked for, so the room treats
the window as before. The answer is the browser's (chrome/browser/spatiand/describe.cc), as the Rust
SpatiMesh gave it: the active tab's title and address, its headings, its words, and the field being
typed in last, the focus followed into frames of the same origin; never what is in a password or
one-time-code field. An answer by 800 ms, without the page's part if the page has not given it.

The protocol's XML is a copy of Spatiand's (third_party/wayland-protocols/spatiand): copied again
when that one changes.

Checked in Spatiand's snapshot room (SPATIAND_STEPS `describe`, 2026-11-10): a page with two
headings, a password field and a message box; with the message box focused the answer ended
"Message: Hello Wor", its vocabulary the headings then the names (SpatiQuill, SpatiShelf, ...); with
the password field focused, no field at all and the password nowhere in it.
